The Wine loader declares itself a game that supports Game Mode, so macOS can give a full-screen Windows game Game Mode.

This repository's patch to the loader's Info.plist (version 1). It adds three keys to loader/wine_info.plist.in, the
Info.plist the linker puts in the loader's __TEXT,__info_plist section (configure.ac's -sectcreate) and patch 0006
rewrites per process for the game's name:
- LSApplicationCategoryType public.app-category.games: the app is a game;
- LSSupportsGameMode true (macOS 26 and later; Apple: "If you don't include this key in your Info.plist, Game Mode
  might not turn on for your game");
- GCSupportsGameMode true, its older name for macOS 14 to 25 (deprecated, still read there; Apple's developer
  support names it with the category as the two steps).
They sit after CFBundleVersion, outside the CFBundleName string and its padding that 0006 rewrites, so 0006's
rewrite is unchanged. The preloader, where configure builds one, gets the same section.

Why: macOS turns Game Mode on for a game in full screen only (Apple's developer support: it "is automatically
disabled if the game isn't running full screen"), and it knows an app is a game that wants Game Mode from these
Info.plist keys. Wine's loader declared none, so a Windows game never got Game Mode: the Metal HUD read "Game Mode
Off" in a full-screen Wine game, and gamepolicyd logged nothing over a whole measured block (mavrik S192, S195,
S210). Game Mode gives the game priority on the CPU and GPU and doubles the Bluetooth sampling rate for game
controllers and AirPods, which matters for the pads that patches 0035 and 0036 bring in. A Windows program that
isn't a game gets nothing from the keys unless it goes full screen; the player can still turn Game Mode off from
the menu bar.

Checked (mavrik S217 lab): applies after patches 0001 to 0036 with no fuzz; the loader builds with the engine's
toolchain with no warning, and its __TEXT,__info_plist section, read back from the built and stripped loader,
parses with the three keys and every other key as before. Whether macOS honours keys in an embedded Info.plist (the
loader is not an .app) is checked live: the Metal HUD's Game Mode line and macOS's own log, in Wine's full screen
and in a macOS full-screen Space.

diff --git a/loader/wine_info.plist.in b/loader/wine_info.plist.in
index 3b13093..b23d631 100644
--- a/loader/wine_info.plist.in
+++ b/loader/wine_info.plist.in
@@ -22,6 +22,12 @@
     <string>????</string>
     <key>CFBundleVersion</key>
     <string>@PACKAGE_VERSION@</string>
+    <key>GCSupportsGameMode</key>
+    <true/>
+    <key>LSApplicationCategoryType</key>
+    <string>public.app-category.games</string>
+    <key>LSSupportsGameMode</key>
+    <true/>
     <key>NSPrincipalClass</key>
     <string>WineApplication</string>
     <key>LSUIElement</key>
